\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The $s^{\ast }$-sweep. The first block is the design $\rho =0$, the only one on which \ref {B:dim} fails; the second collects the rows of the other three designs at which anything happens at all --- at every row not shown, $4p\min _\lambda \mathrm  {Gap}\in [0.899,1.006]$ and $C_\lambda \leq 1.43$. Slacks are in nats, as in \cref  {tab:sec7}; the entry \emph  {---} is $s^{\ast }=1$, where \ref {B:dim} is vacuous. The full table is in \texttt  {sec7\_sstar.txt}.}}{25}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sstar}{{3}{25}{The $s^{\ast }$-sweep. The first block is the design $\rho =0$, the only one on which \ref {B:dim} fails; the second collects the rows of the other three designs at which anything happens at all --- at every row not shown, $4p\min _\lambda \mathrm {Gap}\in [0.899,1.006]$ and $C_\lambda \leq 1.43$. Slacks are in nats, as in \cref {tab:sec7}; the entry \emph {---} is $s^{\ast }=1$, where \ref {B:dim} is vacuous. The full table is in \texttt {sec7\_sstar.txt}}{table.3}{}}
